{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>A psalm of Asaph. O Elohim, nations have come</b> — I mentioned the dispute among the commentators at the beginning of the book. Some say: a psalm is something sung and selected from many; perhaps these were laments, or the meaning of 'a psalm' is that he saw in the Holy Spirit on account of what he wrote at the end, for Israel are His people and His inheritance." "<b>O Elohim</b> — the meaning: how is He Elohim, and the hand of men overpowered His devout ones and the place of His sanctuary?" "<b>Your inheritance</b> — the land of Israel." "<b>For ruins</b> — low places, and the opposite of this: 'the mountain of the house of YHWH shall be established.' And some say: a place where there is no settlement, or they dug up Jerusalem to search for hidden treasures."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 79, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:25.068159726Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}